# afwdev (Python)

## Layout
- Entry: `src/afw_dev/afwdev.py` (also invoked as `./afwdev` from package root).
- Package: `src/afw_dev/_afwdev/` with `generate/`, `build/`, `test/`, `validate/`, `common/`.
- Subcommand metadata uses `_info_<subcommand>` dicts in `afwdev.py` (argparse-driven). Match existing patterns when adding options or subcommands.

## Generate pipeline
- Orchestration: `_afwdev/generate/generate.py` — wipes `src/<srcdir>/generated/` then runs bindings, interfaces, strings, cmake fragments, etc.
- Generators must write only under `generated/` (or documented outputs). Never instruct agents to patch generated C/headers by hand.

## Conventions
- Follow surrounding Python style in `_afwdev` (existing modules are the style guide).
- Use `afw-package.json` / `package` helpers in `_afwdev.common` for srcdir discovery; respect `--srcdir-pattern`.
- Prefer extending an existing generator module over duplicating logic.
- Optional per-srcdir hook: `generate/additional_generate/additional_generate.py`.

## Related commands agents run
```bash
# Use ./afwdev when the build installs/refreshes afwdev itself
./afwdev build --cdev -j
afwdev test -j
afwdev validate --pattern '...'
./afwdev build --all --install -j   # full repo including JS + docs
```
